WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.479 --> 00:00:06.850
At precisely 9 AM each morning, the muffled
voice of a woman can be heard greeting her

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:14.750
‘comrades’ across the border.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:21.690
The source – this wall of 48 speakers built
in 1967 – then proceeds to broadcast a series

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:28.859
of pop songs.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:33.760
The ‘comrades’ she’s referring to are
not Korean, but Chinese.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.430
And the woman, the late Taiwanese pop star
Teresa Teng.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.910
This 3-story propaganda station lies on the
north-western tip of one of Taiwan’s Kinmen

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:51.800
islands – just three miles from the Chinese
mainland and an hour by plane from Taipei.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.840
Kinmen, in other words, lies on the most fraught
edge of an already fraught region.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:07.020
In fact, not once but twice has it successfully
repelled Chinese invasions – in 1949 and

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.020
50.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:13.939
But while the Korean border has largely remained
frozen in time – a combustible buffer zone

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:19.159
that few dare cross, this one has changed
dramatically.

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:25.200
Today, this is what life looks like in the
sleepy villages of Kinmen – home to about

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.140
100,000 people.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.320
On the other side of the narrow channel that
divides them – and visible to the naked

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.380
eye – this is the Chinese city of Xiamen
– population: 5 million.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:44.740
As China’s economic and military strength
has grown, Taiwan has been forced to confront

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.950
its vulnerability.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:52.829
Kinmen would be among the first and easiest
territory to capture – possibly in a matter

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:55.490
of hours.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:01.799
Simple pragmatism, therefore, has slowly transformed
this frontier from a highly-fortified garrison

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:05.820
to a kind of commercialized museum.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:11.940
Once home to 100,000 troops, a mere 3,000
remain today.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:18.860
In their place, 984,000 tourists – most
of them Chinese – arrived in 2019 alone,

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.640
spending about $360 million U.S. Dollars,
and then returning by way of a 20-minute ferry.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:31.240
The broadcast station still plays propaganda,
but at a much lower volume, and only for the

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.450
benefit of tourists.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:39.140
Meanwhile, this tiny patch of land – little
more than a rock – is one of its few active

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.710
military bases.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:45.820
Its usefulness was recently questioned after
it struggled to shoot down a small, consumer

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.790
Chinese drone.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:55.980
Now, make no mistake – an attack on Taiwan’s
main island of Formosa would be no easy feat.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.230
The landscape is mountainous, the 80-mile
journey treacherous, and the weather, frequently

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.599
uncooperative.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:08.850
Still, the extreme vulnerability of Kinmen
is a powerful reminder of Taiwan’s dependence

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:14.780
on the elephant in the room: the United States.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:20.760
